    "https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/fsc_dean_07_2026/": {
      "title": "Dean of Faculty of Science",
      "description": "Dean of Faculty of Science – Career@UM Skip to content Search for: Home Login Career Page Career Opportunities Learn More Contact Us ENG 中文 Home Login Career Page Career Opportunities Learn More Contact Us ENG 中文 View Larger Image Dean of Faculty of Science Dean of Faculty of Science Science (Reference No.: FSC/DEAN/07/2026) Academic Staff The University of Macau sincerely invites applications for the position of the Dean of Faculty of Science . Faculty of Science The Faculty of Science was restructured and reorganized from the Faculty of Science and Technology. Its establishment aligns with the strategic needs of the country and the Macao SAR and will provide foundational support in the basic sciences for technological innovation in Macao and nationwide. The Faculty will comprise the Department of Mathematics, the Department of Physics, the Department of Chemistry, and the Department of Biological Sciences, and is expected to enrol approximately 1,000 students. Dean of Faculty of Science The successful candidate should have considerable experience in faculty management, academic strategic planning, curriculum design, laboratory setup and research development, and must be highly committed to the pursuit of excellence in teaching, research and service. In particular, the candidates should have the following credentials: An earned doctoral degree in Science or related disciplines; A distinguished record of internationally-recognized research and scholarship; Evidence of outstanding academic leadership, demonstrated commitment to leading research and a record of effective teaching in higher education settings; Ability to foster interdisciplinary collaboration, drive technological innovation, and establish relationship with diverse stakeholders; Excellent management and communication skills; Proficiency in English is required as it is the working language, while knowledge in Chinese/Portuguese will be an advantage. Remuneration Remuneration will be commensurate with the successful applicants’ academic qualification and relevant professional experience. The current local maximum income tax rate is 12% but is effectively around 5% – 7% after various discretionary exemptions. Apart from competitive remuneration, UM offers a wide range of benefits, such as medical insurance, provident fund, on-campus accommodation/housing allowance and other subsidies. Further details on our package are available at: https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/learn-more/ . Application Procedure More details about the job vacancy can be accessed at https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/ . The University has appointed Perrett Laver to provide consultancy service for the recruitment of this position. A cover letter, detailed curriculum vitae in English and other related materials should be sent to the following address, with quotation of reference no. FSC/DEAN/07/2026 . 1901 Wilson House, 19-27 Wyndham Street, Central, Hong Kong Email: Matthew.Foreman@perrettlaver.com Tel: +852 3702 6498 Interested individuals are encouraged to submit their materials as early as possible to ensure timely consideration. Review of applications and nominations will commence immediately and continue until the position is filled. Applicants may consider their applications not successful if they are not invited for an interview within 3 months of submission. For enquiries, please call Dr. Matthew Foreman on +852 3702 6498. ***Personal data provided by applicants will be kept confidential and used for recruitment purpose only*** ** Under the equal condition of qualifications and experience, priority will be given to Macao permanent residents** Word document Word document (zip) PDF (view with Acrobat Reader) Download the application form only when applying through this online system is not likely. When not applying through this website, besides completing the application form, please submit your CV, copy of academic certificates (diplomas), ID or passport copy and declaration of employment (for civil servant only) to the above postal address, e-mail address or fax no. Click here to download the Acrobat Reader michelleieong Ieong Lam Ian 2026-09-03T23:42:43+08:00 This site is best viewed in Google Chrome, Mozilla Firefox, Safari or Microsoft Edge. Copyright © Office of Administration (ADMO). All rights reserved.    | UM Home | UM News | UM Event Calendar Page load link Go to Top"
    },
    "https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/fmd_dcm_hod_06_2026/": {
      "title": "Head of Department of Clinical Medicine",
      "description": "Head of Department of Clinical Medicine – Career@UM Skip to content Search for: Home Login Career Page Career Opportunities Learn More Contact Us ENG 中文 Home Login Career Page Career Opportunities Learn More Contact Us ENG 中文 View Larger Image Head of Department of Clinical Medicine Apply for this job now Head of Department of Clinical Medicine Clinical Medicine (Reference No.: FMD/DCM/HOD/06/2026) Academic Staff The newly established Faculty of Medicine at the University of Macau (UM) invites applications for the position of the Head of Department of Clinical Medicine. This recruitment supports the establishment of the new Department of Clinical Medicine, which will focus on precision‑based disease management, clinical technology innovation, and medical quality and safety systems. As part of UM’s broader academic development plan, the University is undertaking a major structural expansion through the restructuring and establishment of five faculties in science and technology. Among them, the Faculty of Medicine (FMD) will be formed based on relevant programmes within the current Faculty of Health Sciences (FHS) and Institute of Chinese Medical Sciences (ICMS) . Building on three established departments─Biomedical Sciences, Pharmaceutical Sciences and Public Health and Medicinal Administration─FMD is establishing a new Department of Clinical Medicine (DCM).  The department will advance the integration of clinical practice, education, and research, and support the development of high‑quality healthcare services. It will play a key role in training clinically competent, research‑informed, and ethically grounded medical professionals, contributing to the advancement of an internationalized healthcare system in Macao and the Greater Bay Area. The appointment will be made at the rank of Professor or above. The successful candidate will provide strategic leadership for the establishment and long‑term development of DCM’s clinical, educational, and research missions. Responsibilities include leading the formation of departmental structures, programmes, and priorities; guiding growth from its inception; fostering integration across core functions; and ensuring alignment with the strategies of FMD and UM. As a founding Head, the appointee will lead the initiation of academic, clinical, and collaborative initiatives, build effective internal and external partnerships, and strengthen engagement with clinical and healthcare institutions. The candidate should possess the following qualifications: 1. An undergraduate degree in clinical medicine from a recognized medical school, preferably with a valid medical registration in Macao, Hong Kong or Chinese Mainland; 2. A doctoral degree (PhD, MD or equivalent) in subdisciplines of clinical medicine or specialties; 3. An outstanding track record of internationally recognized research, scholarship, or clinical innovation; 4. A proven record of excellence in teaching and medical education; 5. Demonstrated competence in academic leadership, management, planning, and communication, including experience in leading departments, units, or major programmes; 6. Relevant hospital‑based clinical experience is an advantage. The selected candidate is expected to assume duty in 2026/2027. Remuneration Remuneration will be commensurate with the successful applicants’ academic qualification and relevant professional experience. The current local maximum income tax rate is 12% but is effectively around 5% – 7% after various discretionary exemptions. Apart from competitive remuneration, UM offers a wide range of benefits, such as medical insurance, provident fund, on-campus accommodation/housing allowance and other subsidies. Further details on our package are available at: https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/learn-more/ . Application Procedure Applicants should visit https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/ for more details, and apply ONLINE . Applicant should submit a cover letter along with a detailed Curriculum Vitae . Review of applications will commence immediately and continue until the position is filled. Applicants may consider their applications not successful if they are not invited for an interview within 3 months of application. Human Resources Section, Office of Administration University of Macau, Av. da Universidade, Taipa, Macau, China Website: https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/ ;  Email: vacancy@um.edu.mo Tel: +853 8822 8589;  Fax: +853 8822 2412 The effective position and salary index are subject to the Personnel Statute of the University of Macau in force. The University of Macau reserves the right not to appoint a candidate. Applicants with less qualification and experience can be offered lower positions under special circumstances. ***Personal data provided by applicants will be kept confidential and used for recruitment purpose only*** ** Under the equal condition of qualifications and experience, priority will be given to Macao permanent residents** Word document Word document (zip) PDF (view with Acrobat Reader) Download the application form only when applying through this online system is not likely. When not applying through this website, besides completing the application form, please submit your CV, copy of academic certificates (diplomas), ID or passport copy and declaration of employment (for civil servant only) to the above postal address, e-mail address or fax no. Click here to download the Acrobat Reader ivylouunin Lou Un In 2026-09-03T23:42:55+08:00 This site is best viewed in Google Chrome, Mozilla Firefox, Safari or Microsoft Edge. Copyright © Office of Administration (ADMO). All rights reserved.    | UM Home | UM News | UM Event Calendar Page load link Go to Top"
    },
    "https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/fss_dcom_hod_10_2025/": {
      "title": "Head of Department of Communication",
      "description": "Head of Department of Communication – Career@UM Skip to content Search for: Home Login Career Page Career Opportunities Learn More Contact Us ENG 中文 Home Login Career Page Career Opportunities Learn More Contact Us ENG 中文 View Larger Image Head of Department of Communication Head of Department of Communication Communication (Reference No.: FSS/DCOM/HOD/10/2025) Academic Staff The Faculty of Social Sciences invites applications for the position of the Head of Department of Communication (at the rank of Professor, Distinguished Professor or Chair Professor) . The Department of Communication The Department offers programmes at the undergraduate and graduate levels, including Bachelor of Social Sciences in Communication, Master of Arts in Communication and New Media, and PhD in Communication Studies. Programmes offered by the Department cover a range of areas across communication, including media studies, journalism, public relations, marketing, digital journalism, and creative media. Teaching expertise is complemented through research expertise in the areas of media and journalism, public relations, public communication, qualitative and quantitative media analysis, cultural studies and intercultural communication. More information about the Department is available on the UM website: https://comm.fss.um.edu.mo/about/ . The Head of Department The Faculty of Social Sciences seeks to appoint an internationally accomplished scholar to lead the Department of Communication. The appointment will be made at the rank of Professor, Distinguished Professor or Chair Professor. The candidate should have strong credentials including an international research profile, a distinguished record of academic achievements, exceptional leadership and management skills, and strategic vision. While the post is open to all areas and methodological approaches of media and communication studies, we are especially interested in candidates with an established international reputation and whose academic expertise is relevant to the concerns of Macao and the Greater China region. The successful candidate will possess: A PhD degree in communication, mass communication, media studies, or related fields; Expertise and knowledge in one or more sub-disciplines such as research methodology, journalism, advertising, public relations, new media, and/or international/intercultural communication; An outstanding record of internationally-recognized research and scholarship; A proven record of excellent teaching; Demonstrable competence in management, planning, and communication; Ability to play a leadership role in the Department; Proficiency in English is required as it is the working language, while knowledge in Chinese or Portuguese will be an advantage. Remuneration Remuneration will be commensurate with the successful applicants’ academic qualification and relevant professional experience. The current local maximum income tax rate is 12% but is effectively around 5% – 7% after various discretionary exemptions. Apart from competitive remuneration, UM offers a wide range of benefits, such as medical insurance, provident fund, on-campus accommodation/housing allowance and other subsidies. Further details on our package are available at: https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/learn-more/ . Application Procedure More details about the job vacancy can be accessed at https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/ . The University has appointed Perrett Laver to provide consultancy service for the recruitment of this position. A cover letter, detailed curriculum vitae in English and other related materials should be sent to the following address, with quotation of reference no. FSS/DCOM/HOD/10/2025 . 1901 Wilson House, 19-27 Wyndham Street, Central, Hong Kong Email: Matthew.Foreman@perrettlaver.com Tel: +852 3702 6497 Interested individuals are encouraged to submit their materials as early as possible to ensure timely consideration. Review of applications and nominations will commence immediately and continue until the position is filled. Applicants may consider their applications not successful if they are not invited for an interview within 3 months of submission. For enquiries, please call Mr. Matthew Foreman on +852 3702 6498. ***Personal data provided by applicants will be kept confidential and used for recruitment purpose only*** ** Under the equal condition of qualifications and experience, priority will be given to Macao permanent residents** Word document Word document (zip) PDF (view with Acrobat Reader) Download the application form only when applying through this online system is not likely. When not applying through this website, besides completing the application form, please submit your CV, copy of academic certificates (diplomas), ID or passport copy and declaration of employment (for civil servant only) to the above postal address, e-mail address or fax no. Click here to download the Acrobat Reader dorachau Chau I Cheng 2026-09-03T23:43:17+08:00 This site is best viewed in Google Chrome, Mozilla Firefox, Safari or Microsoft Edge. Copyright © Office of Administration (ADMO). All rights reserved.    | UM Home | UM News | UM Event Calendar Page load link Go to Top"
    },
    "https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/fah_dpt_hod_06_2026/": {
      "title": "Head of Department of Portuguese",
      "description": "Head of Department of Portuguese – Career@UM Skip to content Search for: Home Login Career Page Career Opportunities Learn More Contact Us ENG 中文 Home Login Career Page Career Opportunities Learn More Contact Us ENG 中文 View Larger Image Head of Department of Portuguese Apply for this job now Head of Department of Portuguese Portuguese (Reference No.: FAH/DPT/HOD/06/2026) Academic Staff The Faculty of Arts and Humanities invites applications for the position of Head of Department of Portuguese (at the rank of Full/Associate Professor). The Department of Portuguese is an established and lively scholarly community. The Department offers an undergraduate degree in Portuguese Studies concentrating on Portuguese with selected courses in Language, Linguistics, Literature, Culture, History and Translation. At the undergraduate level, the Department also teaches Portuguese language within the Faculty of Law and offers elective courses in Portuguese as a foreign language to students from all faculties of the University. At the postgraduate level, the Department offers two Master programmes (i) Portuguese Language and Intercultural Studies; (ii) Translation Studies (Portuguese-Chinese), as well as one PhD programme covering various areas of Portuguese Studies. Qualifications The successful applicant will possess: A PhD in any area of Portuguese Studies: Linguistics, Literature, Culture, Translation or Language Teaching, or related areas; Demonstrable competence in departmental management, planning, and communication, along with the ability to provide leadership within the Department; An outstanding track record of internationally recognized research and scholarship; Experience and success in supervising postgraduate students and a proven track record of excellence in teaching; Native or near-native fluency in Portuguese and the experience in teaching the above-mentioned subjects; A good command of English; knowledge of Chinese is an advantage. The selected candidate is expected to assume duty in 2027. Remuneration A taxable annual remuneration starting from MOP1,052,800 (approximately USD129,980) will be commensurate with the successful applicants’ academic qualification and relevant professional experience. The current local maximum income tax rate is 12% but is effectively around 5% – 7% after various discretionary exemptions. Apart from competitive remuneration, UM offers a wide range of benefits, such as medical insurance, provident fund, on-campus accommodation/housing allowance and other subsidies. Further details on our package are available at: https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/learn-more/ . Application Procedure Applicants should visit https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/ for more details, and apply ONLINE . Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. Applicants may consider their applications not successful if they are not invited for an interview within 3 months of application. Human Resources Section, Office of Administration University of Macau, Av. da Universidade, Taipa, Macau, China Website: https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/ ;  Email: vacancy@um.edu.mo Tel: +853 8822 8699;  Fax: +853 8822 2412 The effective position and salary index are subject to the Personnel Statute of the University of Macau in force. The University of Macau reserves the right not to appoint a candidate. Applicants with less qualification and experience can be offered lower positions under special circumstances. ***Personal data provided by applicants will be kept confidential and used for recruitment purpose only*** ** Under the equal condition of qualifications and experience, priority will be given to Macao permanent residents** Word document Word document (zip) PDF (view with Acrobat Reader) Download the application form only when applying through this online system is not likely. When not applying through this website, besides completing the application form, please submit your CV, copy of academic certificates (diplomas), ID or passport copy and declaration of employment (for civil servant only) to the above postal address, e-mail address or fax no. Click here to download the Acrobat Reader ensonho Ho Io San 2026-09-02T23:42:51+08:00 This site is best viewed in Google Chrome, Mozilla Firefox, Safari or Microsoft Edge. Copyright © Office of Administration (ADMO). All rights reserved.    | UM Home | UM News | UM Event Calendar Page load link Go to Top"
    },
    "https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/fmd_pro_faap_09_2026/": {
      "title": "Full/Associate/Assistant Professor in Precision Oncology",
      "description": "Full/Associate/Assistant Professor in Precision Oncology – Career@UM Skip to content Search for: Home Login Career Page Career Opportunities Learn More Contact Us ENG 中文 Full/Associate/Assistant Professor in Precision Oncology Apply for this job now Full/Associate/Assistant Professor in Precision Oncology Precision Oncology (Reference No.: FMD/PRO/FAAP/09/2026) Academic Staff The Faculty of Medicine (FMD) was established in August 2026 through the expansion and restructuring of the former Faculty of Health Sciences. The Faculty’s educational mission is delivered through five academic departments: the Department of Biomedical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Pharmacy and Pharmaceutical Sciences, Department of Public Health and Medicinal Administration, and Department of Medicinal Food and Nutrition Sciences. The Faculty’s research mission is supported by three major research platforms: the Institute of Chinese Medical Sciences, the State Key Laboratory of Mechanism and Quality of Chinese Medicine and the Ministry of Education Frontiers Science Centre for Precision Oncology (FSCPO). Precision oncology is a key strategic research focus of FMD, with FSCPO serving as a flagship platform for advancing translational research from scientific discovery to clinical application. The Faculty of Medicine ( http://fmd.um.edu.mo/ ) and the Ministry of Education Frontiers Science Center for Precision Oncology invite applications for the position of Full, Associate or Assistant Professor in Precision Oncology. Successful candidates will be expected to establish or further develop internationally recognized research programmes in precision oncology, contribute to the educational missions of FMD and FSCPO through teaching and postgraduate supervision, and foster interdisciplinary collaborations within the University and with leading institutions worldwide. The appointment at the rank of Full Professor will be expected to provide academic and strategic leadership to strengthen the research capacity of FSCPO and to work closely with the Director of FSCPO in shaping FSCPO’s future development. Through the leadership roles in both FMD and FSCPO, the successful candidate will help strengthen UM’s position as a leading centre for translational cancer research, innovation, and talent development. Qualifications A doctoral degree in biological sciences, biotechnology, health sciences, medicine, or a related discipline. Candidates are expected to have an internationally recognized track record in RNA biology, cancer biology, and/or drug development for human cancers. Candidate for Assistant Professor should demonstrate strong potential in research and teaching, and a minimum of three years of postdoctoral training is preferred. The appointment at the rank of Full Professor and Associate Professor should demonstrate an established record of research excellence, evidenced by publications in leading international journals, success in securing competitive research funding, editorial board memberships, and invited presentations at major international conferences. Candidates for Full Professor and Associate Professor should also demonstrate academic leadership and the ability to develop internationally competitive research programmes and mentor junior researchers. The selected candidate is expected to assume duty in 2026/2027. Remuneration A taxable annual remuneration starting MOP1,250,200 (approximately USD154,350) for the position of Full Professor; MOP1,052,800 (approximately USD129,980) for the position of Associate Professor and MOP855,400 (approximately USD105,600) for the position of Assistant Professor will be commensurate with the successful applicants’ academic qualification and relevant professional experience. The current local maximum income tax rate is 12% but is effectively around 5% – 7% after various discretionary exemptions. Apart from competitive remuneration, UM offers a wide range of benefits, such as medical insurance, provident fund, on-campus accommodation/housing allowance and other subsidies. Further details on our package are available at: https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/learn-more/ . Application Procedure Applicants should visit https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/ for more details, and apply ONLINE . Applicant should submit a cover letter in which the preferred position(s) is specified, along with a detailed Curriculum Vitae. Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. Applicants may consider their applications not successful if they are not invited for an interview within 3 months of application. Human Resources Section, Office of Administration University of Macau, Av. da Universidade, Taipa, Macau, China Website: https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/ ;  Email: vacancy@um.edu.mo Tel: +853 8822 8589;  Fax: +853 8822 2412 The effective position and salary index are subject to the Personnel Statute of the University of Macau in force. The University of Macau reserves the right not to appoint a candidate. Applicants with less qualification and experience can be offered lower positions under special circumstances. ***Personal data provided by applicants will be kept confidential and used for recruitment purpose only*** ** Under the equal condition of qualifications and experience, priority will be given to Macao permanent residents** Word document Word document (zip) PDF (view with Acrobat Reader) Download the application form only when applying through this online system is not likely. When not applying through this website, besides completing the application form, please submit your CV, copy of academic certificates (diplomas), ID or passport copy and declaration of employment (for civil servant only) to the above postal address, e-mail address or fax no. Click here to download the Acrobat Reader ivylouunin Lou Un In 2026-09-14T23:40:23+08:00 This site is best viewed in Google Chrome, Mozilla Firefox, Safari or Microsoft Edge. Copyright © Office of Administration (ADMO). All rights reserved.    | UM Home | UM News | UM Event Calendar Page load link Go to Top"
    },
    "https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/fmd_rp_09_2026/": {
      "title": "Research Positions in the Faculty of Medicine",
      "description": "Research Positions in the Faculty of Medicine – Career@UM Skip to content Search for: Home Login Career Page Career Opportunities Learn More Contact Us ENG 中文 Home Login Career Page Career Opportunities Learn More Contact Us ENG 中文 Research Positions in the Faculty of Medicine Apply for this job now Research Positions in the Faculty of Medicine -- (Reference No.: FMD/RP/09/2026) Research Staff The Faculty of Medicine (FMD) was established in August 2026 through the expansion and restructuring of the former Faculty of Health Sciences. The Faculty’s educational mission is delivered through five academic departments: the Department of Biomedical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Pharmacy and Pharmaceutical Sciences, Department of Public Health and Medicinal Administration, and Department of Medicinal Food and Nutrition Sciences. The Faculty’s research mission is supported by three major research platforms: the Institute of Chinese Medical Sciences (ICMS), the State Key Laboratory of Mechanism and Quality of Chinese Medicine (SKL-MQCM), and the Ministry of Education Frontiers Science Centre for Precision Oncology (FSCPO). Together, these platforms support a broad spectrum of research activities spanning biomedical sciences, clinical and translational medicine, Chinese medical sciences, and related interdisciplinary fields. Precision oncology is a key strategic research focus of FMD, with FSCPO serving as a flagship platform for advancing translational research from scientific discovery to clinical application. FMD is now recruiting research personnel with extensive research experience in at least one of the ten strategic research directions of FMD: (1) Precision Oncology, (2) Stem Cell and Development, (3) Aging, Neural and Metabolism Disorders and Infectious Diseases, (4) Biomedical Imaging, (5) Data Science, (6) Drug Development, (7) Neuropsychiatry, (8) Structural Biology, (9) Translational Medicine, and (10) Public Health. Initial appointment is up to 12 months with a possibility of renewal upon mutual agreement. Qualifications Visiting Fellows: A doctoral degree and professional rank at Associate Professor or above in related disciplines; a solid research record and expertise. Research Assistant Professors: A doctoral degree in relevant disciplines, with a proven track record of research publications and achievements. Post-doctoral research experience is highly desirable. Postdoctoral Fellows: A doctoral degree in related disciplines; a solid record of publication and scientific training. Research Assistants: A bachelor’s degree or above in related disciplines with solid research experience in health science-related studies. The selected candidate is expected to assume duty as soon as possible. Remuneration Remuneration and appointment rank offered will be competitive and commensurate with the successful applicants’ academic qualification and relevant professional experience. The current local maximum income tax rate is 12% but is effectively around 5% – 7% after various discretionary exemptions. Application Procedure Applicants should visit https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/ for more details, and apply ONLINE . Review of applications will continue until the positions are filled. Applicants may consider their applications not successful if they are not invited for an interview within 3 months of application. Human Resources Section, Office of Administration University of Macau, Av. da Universidade, Taipa, Macau, China Website: https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/ ;  Email: vacancy@um.edu.mo Tel: +853 8822 8589;  Fax: +853 8822 2412 The University of Macau reserves the right not to appoint a candidate. ***Personal data provided by applicants will be kept confidential and used for recruitment purpose only*** ** Under the equal condition of qualifications and experience, priority will be given to Macao permanent residents**a Word document Word document (zip) PDF (view with Acrobat Reader) Download the application form only when applying through this online system is not likely. When not applying through this website, besides completing the application form, please submit your CV, copy of academic certificates (diplomas), ID or passport copy and declaration of employment (for civil servant only) to the above postal address, e-mail address or fax no. Click here to download the Acrobat Reader ivylouunin Lou Un In 2026-09-14T23:40:21+08:00 This site is best viewed in Google Chrome, Mozilla Firefox, Safari or Microsoft Edge. Copyright © Office of Administration (ADMO). All rights reserved.    | UM Home | UM News | UM Event Calendar Page load link Go to Top"
    },
    "https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/cmdo_sfs_dr_09_2026/": {
      "title": "誠聘司機",
      "description": "誠聘司機 – Career@UM Skip to content Search for: Home Login Career Page Career Opportunities Learn More Contact Us ENG 中文 Home Login Career Page Career Opportunities Learn More Contact Us ENG 中文 誠聘司機 Apply for this job now 誠聘司機 - (Reference No.: CMDO/SFS/DR/09/2026) Administrative Staff 澳門大學校園管理及發展部保安及設施服務處現招聘司機(技術工人職級)，可課稅月薪由澳門元15,040.00至28,200.00 (薪俸點160至300)。 職務性質 負責駕駛輕型汽車、貨車及25座位或以下小巴； 向校內各部門提供公務上的接載服務； 向本校師生、職員及賓客提供小巴接載服務； 協助辦公室文件遞送工作； 按制定的指引每天對車輛進行基本檢查，以確保大學車輛處於良好狀態； 按需要跨境工作； 執行其他特別指派之職務。 職位要求 澳門特別行政區永久性居民； 具初中畢業或以上學歷； 持本地有效重型客車駕駛執照(D1或D2手動排檔)及中華人民共和國機動車駕駛證(C1)； 具有效澳門機動車入出橫琴駕駛人申請資格； 具有最少5年之本地全職客車司機駕駛工作經驗； 具有保持車輛於良好狀態之知識； 願意超時工作； 懂普通話及簡單英語為佳。 申請程序 應徵者應透過 https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/ 瀏覽詳情及於 2026年10月15日 或之前連同個人履歷、學歷證明文件副本、有效本地重型客車駕駛執照副本、有效中華人民共和國機動車駕駛證副本及澳門居民身份證副本 在線 遞交申請。上述職位要求將作為申請篩選之用途，應徵者請於履歷及職位申請表上清楚列明所取得之學歷及描述其相關工作內容。聯絡方式如下: 中國澳門氹仔大學大馬路 澳門大學行政部人力資源處 網頁： https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/ 電子郵箱： vacancy@um.edu.mo 電話： +853 8822 8574 傳真： +853 8822 2412 實際聘任的職位及薪俸點根據《澳門大學人員通則》的規定訂定。澳門大學保留不聘用任何候選人的權力。特殊情況下，資歷及經驗不足的應聘者可以較低職位聘用。 ***個人資料將受嚴格保密並僅用於招聘事宜*** Word document Download the application form only when applying through this online system is not likely. When not applying through this website, besides completing the application form, please submit your CV, copy of academic certificates (diplomas), copy of academic transcripts, ID or passport copy and declaration of employment (for civil servant only) to the above postal address, e-mail address or fax no. alisonwong Wong Weng I 2026-09-24T23:42:08+08:00 This site is best viewed in Google Chrome, Mozilla Firefox, Safari or Microsoft Edge. Copyright © Office of Administration (ADMO). All rights reserved.    | UM Home | UM News | UM Event Calendar Page load link Go to Top"
    },
    "https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/fsc_bio_ai_faap_09_2026/": {
      "title": "Full/Associate/Assistant Professor in AI for Biomolecular Design",
      "description": "Full/Associate/Assistant Professor in AI for Biomolecular Design – Career@UM Skip to content Search for: Home Login Career Page Career Opportunities Learn More Contact Us ENG 中文 Full/Associate/Assistant Professor in AI for Biomolecular Design Apply for this job now Full/Associate/Assistant Professor in AI for Biomolecular Design Biology (Reference No.: FSC/BIO/AI/FAAP/09/2026) Academic Staff The Faculty of Science at the University of Macau (UM) invites applications for the position of Full/Associate/Assistant Professor in AI for Biomolecular Design. This recruitment supports the launch of the new Department of Biological Sciences, part of UM’s strategic initiative to strengthen its foundation in fundamental and applied sciences. As part of UM’s broader academic development plan, the university undertook a major structural expansion by restructuring and establishing five faculties in science and technology. Among them, the Faculty of Science was formed based on relevant program of the formerly Faculty of Science and Technology (now Faculty of Engineering, Faculty of Information Science and Computing, and Faculty of Science) and the formerly Faculty of Health Sciences (now Faculty of Medicine). The new Faculty includes the Department of Biological Sciences, Department of Chemistry, Department of Physics, and Department of Mathematics. The establishment of the Department of Biological Sciences will enhance the faculty’s multidisciplinary ecosystem and foster cross-cutting collaborations in emerging areas of science and technology. (For more details, please visit https://fsc.um.edu.mo/ and https://fmd.um.edu.mo /). The Department of Biological Sciences strives to excel in both fundamental and applied research in biological sciences, particularly in areas of omics, computational biology, AI-driven biology, and generative biology. We seek candidates with expertise in these areas, especially those whose research leverages computational and AI technologies to address fundamental biological questions. Successful candidates are expected to contribute to undergraduate and postgraduate teaching, curriculum development, and student mentorship, while establishing internationally competitive research programs. Qualifications Applicants should hold a PhD in disciplines closely related to the areas specified above, preferably with a strong background in AI for Biomolecular Design. The successful candidate is expected to demonstrate a strong publication record, the ability to establish and lead an impactful research program addressing significant biological questions, a commitment to high-quality teaching at both undergraduate and postgraduate levels, and active contribution to the development and growth of the Department and Faculty. The selected candidate is expected to assume duty in Fall 2026 or Spring 2027. Remuneration A taxable annual remuneration starting from MOP1,250,200 (approximately USD154,350) for the position of Full Professor, MOP1,052,800 (approximately USD129,980) for the position of Associate Professor and MOP855,400 (approximately USD105,600) for the position of Assistant Professor will be commensurate with the successful applicants’ academic qualification and relevant professional experience. The current local maximum income tax rate is 12% but is effectively around 5% – 7% after various discretionary exemptions. Apart from competitive remuneration, UM offers a wide range of benefits, such as medical insurance, provident fund, on-campus accommodation/housing allowance and other subsidies. Further details on our package are available at: https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/learn-more/ . Application Procedure Applicants should visit https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/ for more details, and apply ONLINE . Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. Applicants may consider their applications not successful if they are not invited for an interview within 3 months of application. Human Resources Section, Office of Administration University of Macau, Av. da Universidade, Taipa, Macau, China Website: https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/ ;  Email: vacancy@um.edu.mo Tel: +853 8822 8690;  Fax: +853 8822 2412 The effective position and salary index are subject to the Personnel Statute of the University of Macau in force. The University of Macau reserves the right not to appoint a candidate. Applicants with less qualification and experience can be offered lower positions under special circumstances. ***Personal data provided by applicants will be kept confidential and used for recruitment purpose only*** ** Under the equal condition of qualifications and experience, priority will be given to Macao permanent residents** Word document Word document (zip) PDF (view with Acrobat Reader) Download the application form only when applying through this online system is not likely. When not applying through this website, besides completing the application form, please submit your CV, copy of academic certificates (diplomas), ID or passport copy and declaration of employment (for civil servant only) to the above postal address, e-mail address or fax no. Click here to download the Acrobat Reader kasperso So Ka Chon 2026-09-24T23:42:06+08:00 This site is best viewed in Google Chrome, Mozilla Firefox, Safari or Microsoft Edge. Copyright © Office of Administration (ADMO). All rights reserved.    | UM Home | UM News | UM Event Calendar Page load link Go to Top"
    },
    "https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/isct_rp_09_2026/": {
      "title": "Research Positions for the Institute of Smart City Technologies",
      "description": "Research Positions for the Institute of Smart City Technologies – Career@UM Skip to content Search for: Home Login Career Page Career Opportunities Learn More Contact Us ENG 中文 Home Login Career Page Career Opportunities Learn More Contact Us ENG 中文 Research Positions for the Institute of Smart City Technologies Apply for this job now Research Positions for the Institute of Smart City Technologies Smart City Technologies (Reference No.: ISCT/RP/09/2026) Research Staff The Institute of Smart City Technologies (ISCT), established in 2026 as an independent academic unit of the University of Macau, advances smart-city development through education, research, innovation, and technology transfer. Working closely with the State Key Laboratory of Internet of Things for Smart City (IOTSC), ISCT conducts research in IoT, artificial intelligence, big data, and smart-city engineering. Through interdisciplinary collaboration, talent cultivation, and industry partnerships, ISCT develops innovative solutions to promote urban sustainability, enhance quality of life, and support innovation-driven development in Macao and the Greater Bay Area. More details about the Institute of Smart City Technologies are available from https://isct.um.edu.mo/ . ISCT is now recruiting research personnel with extensive research experience in at least one of the following areas: (1) Intelligent Sensing and Network Communication; (2) Urban Big Data and Intelligent Technology; (3) Smart Energy; (4) Intelligent Transportation; (5) Urban Safety and Disaster Prevention; (6) Technology Promotion and Knowledge Transfer; (7) Data Analytics and Smart City Applications. Initial appointment is up to 12 months with a possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and mutual agreement. Qualifications Postdoctoral Fellows: A doctoral degree in relevant disciplines; a solid record of publication and scientific training. Research Assistants: A bachelor’s degree or above in relevant disciplines; a solid record of scientific training with relevant research experience. The selected candidate is expected to assume duty as soon as possible. Remuneration Remuneration and appointment rank offered will be commensurate with the successful applicants’ academic qualification and relevant professional experience. The current local maximum income tax rate is 12% but is effectively around 5% – 7% after various discretionary exemptions. Basic medical benefits are available at a low cost. Application Procedure Applicants should visit https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/ for more details and apply ONLINE . Review of applications will continue until the positions are filled. Applicants may consider their applications not successful if they are not invited for an interview within 3 months of application. Human Resources Section, Office of Administration University of Macau, Av. da Universidade, Taipa, Macau, China Website: https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/ ; Email: vacancy@um.edu.mo Tel: +853 8822 8577; Fax: +853 8822 2412 The University of Macau reserves the right not to appoint a candidate. ***Personal data provided by applicants will be kept confidential and used for recruitment purpose only*** ** Under the equal condition of qualifications and experience, priority will be given to Macao permanent residents** Word document Word document (zip) PDF (view with Acrobat Reader) Download the application form only when applying through this online system is not likely. When not applying through this website, besides completing the application form, please submit your CV, copy of academic certificates (diplomas), ID or passport copy and declaration of employment (for civil servant only) to the above postal address, e-mail address or fax no. Click here to download the Acrobat Reader kasperso So Ka Chon 2026-09-24T23:42:07+08:00 This site is best viewed in Google Chrome, Mozilla Firefox, Safari or Microsoft Edge. Copyright © Office of Administration (ADMO). All rights reserved.    | UM Home | UM News | UM Event Calendar Page load link Go to Top"
