    "https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/fmd_scbrm_faap_09_2026/": {
      "title": "Full/Associate/Assistant Professor in Stem Cell Biology and Regenerative Medicine",
      "description": "Full/Associate/Assistant Professor in Stem Cell Biology and Regenerative Medicine – Career@UM Skip to content Search for: Home Login Career Page Career Opportunities Learn More Contact Us ENG 中文 Full/Associate/Assistant Professor in Stem Cell Biology and Regenerative Medicine Apply for this job now Full/Associate/Assistant Professor in Stem Cell Biology and Regenerative Medicine Stem Cell Biology and Regenerative Medicine (Reference No.: FMD/SCBRM/FAAP/09/2026) Academic Staff The Faculty of Medicine (FMD) was established in August 2026 through the expansion and restructuring of the former Faculty of Health Sciences. The Faculty’s educational mission is delivered through five academic departments: the Department of Biomedical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Pharmacy and Pharmaceutical Sciences, Department of Public Health and Medicinal Administration, and Department of Medicinal Food and Nutrition Sciences. Stem Cell Biology and Regenerative Medicine is one of the key strategic research focuses of FMD. The Faculty of Medicine ( http://fmd.um.edu.mo/ ) invite applications for the position of Full, Associate, or Assistant Professor in Stem Cell Biology and Regenerative Medicine. Successful candidate will be expected to provide academic and strategic leadership in stem cell biology and regenerative medicine, develop internationally recognizable research programmes, and foster interdisciplinary collaborations within the University and with leading institutions worldwide. Working closely with the current faculty members in this field, the candidate will play a key role in shaping UM’s development, strengthening its research capacity, building high-impact research teams, and advancing translational research. The candidate will also contribute to the Faculty’s educational mission through teaching, postgraduate supervision, and academic programme development. Through the excellence in research, teaching, and services, the successful candidate will help strengthen UM’s position as a leading centre for basic and translational research, innovation, and talent development. Qualifications A doctoral degree in biological sciences, biotechnology, health sciences, medicine, or a related discipline. Candidates are expected to have well-recognized track record in developmental biology, stem cell biology, regenerative medicine, and/or cell and gene therapy, demonstrated through publications in leading international journals. Competence also includes success in obtaining competitive research funding, editorial board memberships, and invited presentations at major international conferences. Preference will be given to candidates whose research is either clinically relevant or has great potential for clinical translation. For Assistant Professor, it is preferable to have three years or above of postdoctoral training. Senior candidates should have demonstrated strong academic leadership, experience in leading interdisciplinary research initiatives, and the ability to build internationally competitive research programmes and mentor junior researchers. The selected candidate is expected to assume duty in 2026/2027. Remuneration A taxable annual remuneration starting MOP1,250,200 (approximately USD154,350) for the position of Full Professor; MOP1,052,800 (approximately USD129,980) for the position of Associate Professor and MOP855,400 (approximately USD105,600) for the position of Assistant Professor will be commensurate with the successful applicants’ academic qualification and relevant professional experience. The current local maximum income tax rate is 12% but is effectively around 5% – 7% after various discretionary exemptions. Apart from competitive remuneration, UM offers a wide range of benefits, such as medical insurance, provident fund, on-campus accommodation/housing allowance and other subsidies. Further details on our package are available at: https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/learn-more/ . Application Procedure Applicants should visit https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/ for more details, and apply ONLINE . Applicant should submit a cover letter in which the preferred position(s) is specified, along with a detailed Curriculum Vitae. Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. Applicants may consider their applications not successful if they are not invited for an interview within 3 months of application. Human Resources Section, Office of Administration University of Macau, Av. da Universidade, Taipa, Macau, China Website: https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/ ;  Email: vacancy@um.edu.mo Tel: +853 8822 8690;  Fax: +853 8822 2412 The effective position and salary index are subject to the Personnel Statute of the University of Macau in force. The University of Macau reserves the right not to appoint a candidate. Applicants with less qualification and experience can be offered lower positions under special circumstances. ***Personal data provided by applicants will be kept confidential and used for recruitment purpose only*** ** Under the equal condition of qualifications and experience, priority will be given to Macao permanent residents** Word document Word document (zip) PDF (view with Acrobat Reader) Download the application form only when applying through this online system is not likely. When not applying through this website, besides completing the application form, please submit your CV, copy of academic certificates (diplomas), ID or passport copy and declaration of employment (for civil servant only) to the above postal address, e-mail address or fax no. Click here to download the Acrobat Reader ivylouunin Lou Un In 2026-09-24T23:42:07+08:00 This site is best viewed in Google Chrome, Mozilla Firefox, Safari or Microsoft Edge. Copyright © Office of Administration (ADMO). All rights reserved.    | UM Home | UM News | UM Event Calendar Page load link Go to Top"
    },
    "https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/fll_ra_10_2026/": {
      "title": "Research Assistant for the Faculty of Law",
      "description": "Research Assistant for the Faculty of Law – Career@UM Skip to content Search for: Home Login Career Page Career Opportunities Learn More Contact Us ENG 中文 Research Assistant for the Faculty of Law Apply for this job now Research Assistant for the Faculty of Law Law (Reference No.: FLL/RA/10/2026) Research Staff The Faculty of Law (FLL) is the longest-established law school in Macao, offering teaching and research in Chinese, Portuguese and English across Macao law, Chinese law, European Union law, international law and comparative law. More details about the Faculty are available at: https://fll.um.edu.mo/ . FLL invites applications for the position of Research Assistant. The appointee will provide research support, including conducting literature and case research, editing and proofreading manuscripts, checking citations and references, liaising with contributors and the publisher, and assisting with other project-related work as required. Initial appointment is up to 12 months with a possibility of renewal upon mutual agreement and funding availability. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree or above in Law or related disciplines. Possession of a Master’s degree or above in Law is strongly preferred; Demonstrated research experience in the field of law and artificial intelligence (Legal AI); Academic or study background in Macao law, such as postgraduate legal studies in Macao or demonstrable coursework/research on the legal system of the Macao SAR; Practical skills in Legal AI development, including the ability to build demo systems from scratch, proficiency in vibe coding, debugging, data processing, and LLM API integration, and familiarity with information retrieval techniques; Strong communication, organizational, problem-solving, and interpersonal skills; Good command of both English and Chinese (Cantonese or Mandarin). The selected candidate is expected to assume duty in January 2027. Remuneration Remuneration offered will be commensurate with the successful applicants’ academic qualification and relevant professional experience. The current local maximum income tax rate is 12% but is effectively around 5% – 7% after various discretionary exemptions. Application Procedure Applicants should visit https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/ for more details, and apply ONLINE . Review of applications will commence on 23 October 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Applicants may consider their applications not successful if they are not invited for an interview within 3 months of application. Human Resources Section, Office of Administration University of Macau, Av. da Universidade, Taipa, Macau, China Website: https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/ ; Email: vacancy@um.edu.mo Tel: +853 8822 8406;  Fax: +853 8822 2412 The University of Macau reserves the right not to appoint a candidate. ***Personal data provided by applicants will be kept confidential and used for recruitment purpose only*** ** Under the equal condition of qualifications and experience, priority will be given to Macao permanent residents** Word document Word document (zip) PDF (view with Acrobat Reader) Download the application form only when applying through this online system is not likely. When not applying through this website, besides completing the application form, please submit your CV, copy of academic certificates (diplomas), ID or passport copy and declaration of employment (for civil servant only) to the above postal address, e-mail address or fax no. Click here to download the Acrobat Reader michelleieong Ieong Lam Ian 2026-10-09T23:40:12+08:00 This site is best viewed in Google Chrome, Mozilla Firefox, Safari or Microsoft Edge. Copyright © Office of Administration (ADMO). All rights reserved.    | UM Home | UM News | UM Event Calendar Page load link Go to Top"
    },
    "https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/ici_ao_saa_10_2026/": {
      "title": "Administrative Officer/Senior Administrative Assistant for the Institute of Collaborative Innovation",
      "description": "Administrative Officer/Senior Administrative Assistant for the Institute of Collaborative Innovation – Career@UM Skip to content Search for: Home Login Career Page Career Opportunities Learn More Contact Us ENG 中文 Administrative Officer/Senior Administrative Assistant for the Institute of Collaborative Innovation Apply for this job now Administrative Officer/Senior Administrative Assistant for the Institute of Collaborative Innovation - (Reference No.: ICI/AO/SAA/10/2026) Administrative Staff The Institute of Collaborative Innovation (ICI) of the University of Macau invites applications for the position of Administrative Officer/Senior Administrative Assistant at a taxable monthly salary ranging from MOP34,780 to MOP52,640 (index 370 – 560). Responsibilities Promote and support technology commercialization and entrepreneurship at UM; Work with and support university academic staff and researchers for technology startups formation, incubation and growth; Engage with industry partners, public sector and investors both locally and overseas to facilitate UM commercialization and entrepreneurship activities; Initiate and organize technology promotion and marketing activities and work in a team for project management and execution; Organize events and manage end-to-end logistics – including forums, exhibitions, workshops, and networking sessions – to support the institute’s programs and outreach efforts; Perform other tasks and ad-hoc duties as assigned. Requirements Bachelor’s degree or above in Science, IT or Engineering. Master’s degree or above is highly preferred; At least 8 years of private sector or research related work experiences; Familiarity with the innovation and entrepreneurship landscape in Greater Bay Area and Chinese Mainland is an asset; Knowledge on IP management and laws in both Macau and Chinese Mainland is a plus; Experience working in an incubator or accelerator is a plus; Excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese (Cantonese and Mandarin); Strategic mindset with good communication, interpersonal, analytical and problem-solving skills. Application Procedure Applicants should visit https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/ for more details and apply ONLINE on or before 22 October 2026 . Application screening will be based on requirements listed above. Please indicate the education qualification obtained and describe relevant work experience clearly in the Curriculum Vitae and application form. The contact points are: Human Resources Section, Office of Administration University of Macau, Av. da Universidade, Taipa, Macau, China Website: https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/;  Email: vacancy@um.edu.mo Tel: +853 8822 8578;  Fax: +853 8822 2412 The effective position and salary index are subject to the Personnel Statute of the University of Macau in force. The University of Macau reserves the right not to appoint a candidate. Applicants with less qualification and experience can be offered lower positions under special circumstances. ***Personal data provided by applicants will be kept confidential and used for recruitment purpose only*** ** Under the equal condition of qualifications and experience, priority will be given to Macao permanent residents** Word document Download the application form only when applying through this online system is not likely. When not applying through this website, besides completing the application form, please submit your CV, copy of academic certificates (diplomas), copy of academic transcripts, ID or passport copy and declaration of employment (for civil servant only) to the above postal address, e-mail address or fax no. dorachau Chau I Cheng 2026-10-09T23:40:15+08:00 This site is best viewed in Google Chrome, Mozilla Firefox, Safari or Microsoft Edge. Copyright © Office of Administration (ADMO). All rights reserved.    | UM Home | UM News | UM Event Calendar Page load link Go to Top"
    },
    "https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/ckyc_aa_10_2026/": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant for the Choi Kai Yau College",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant for the Choi Kai Yau College – Career@UM Skip to content Search for: Home Login Career Page Career Opportunities Learn More Contact Us ENG 中文 Administrative Assistant for the Choi Kai Yau College Apply for this job now Administrative Assistant for the Choi Kai Yau College - (Reference No.: CKYC/AA/10/2026) Administrative Staff The Choi Kai Yau College (CKYC) of the University of Macau (UM) invites applications for the position of Administrative Assistant at a taxable monthly salary ranging from MOP25,380 to MOP33,840 (index 270 – 360). Responsibilities Provide administrative support to the college; Assist in organizing and executing various college events, including formal dining functions, outbound trips, student leadership initiatives and visit activities; Oversee residential operations, including student trainee program, managing mass move-in/out exercises, handling summer stay/luggage storage logistics and maintaining accurate resident and activity records; Handle all college publicity and promotion duties, including updating website content, writing news items and managing promotions across platforms; Prepare and support financial and administrative proposals, reimbursements, procurement processing and general office operations; Liaise with relevant UM units and oversee college facility maintenance, security and cleaning management, and catering services to ensure the smooth operation of the college; Perform other duties as assigned. Requirements Bachelor’s degree or above in Business Administration, Public Administration, Communication, English Studies or related disciplines; At least 2 years of relevant full-time working experience in education institutions, student services, residential management, public administration, event management or related areas; Good written and spoken English and Chinese (Cantonese and Mandarin), with proficiency in Portuguese being an advantage; Competence in MS Office applications, with advanced expertise in MS Excel and basic knowledge of WordPress website management will be an advantage; Experience in handling promotional activities, including managing website content, drafting newsletters and releasing announcements across various platforms will be an advantage; Self-motivated, detail-oriented, with strong multitasking skills and ability to work under pressure and overtime as required. Application Procedure Applicants should visit https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/ for more details and apply ONLINE on or before 22 October 2026 . Application screening will be based on requirements listed above. Please indicate the education qualification obtained and describe relevant work experience clearly in the Curriculum Vitae and application form. The contact points are: Human Resources Section, Office of Administration University of Macau, Av. da Universidade, Taipa, Macau, China Website: https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/ ;  Email: vacancy@um.edu.mo Tel: +853 8822 8406;  Fax: +853 8822 2412 The effective position and salary index are subject to the Personnel Statute of the University of Macau in force. The University of Macau reserves the right not to appoint a candidate. Applicants with less qualification and experience can be offered lower positions under special circumstances. ***Personal data provided by applicants will be kept confidential and used for recruitment purpose only*** ** Under the equal condition of qualifications and experience, priority will be given to Macao permanent residents** Word document Download the application form only when applying through this online system is not likely. When not applying through this website, besides completing the application form, please submit your CV, copy of academic certificates (diplomas), copy of academic transcripts, ID or passport copy and declaration of employment (for civil servant only) to the above postal address, e-mail address or fax no. michelleieong Ieong Lam Ian 2026-10-09T23:40:16+08:00 This site is best viewed in Google Chrome, Mozilla Firefox, Safari or Microsoft Edge. Copyright © Office of Administration (ADMO). All rights reserved.    | UM Home | UM News | UM Event Calendar Page load link Go to Top"
